        <tr>
          <td style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 2pt 2pt 2pt 3pt; vertical-align: top" colspan="7">
                        <p class="CellBody">2.&nbsp;Planned Residential Developments in the Community Commercial (CC) and Neighborhood Community Commercial (NCC) zones shall utilize the Medium Density Residential (MR) zone development standards.</p>

          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
</table>
            <p class="P1">D.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="bold">Required Design Elements.</span></p>

            <p class="P2">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A Planned Residential Development shall include one or more of the following design elements that equal or exceed a sum of five points. The elected design elements are at the discretion of the subdivider and shall be identified on the approved final plat.</p>

            <p class="P2">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The Planning Director shall determine compliance with the design elements elected.</p>

            <p class="P2">3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Each subdivision plat shall include a Planned Residential Development agreement that details how each elected design element will be implemented to the satisfaction of the Planning Director. The agreement shall be recorded in conjunction with the subdivision plat.</p>

            <p class="P3">a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Subdivision includes the provision of at least 10 percent of all residential units as Category 1 Affordable Housing (five points).</p>

            <p class="P3">b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A street network that includes alleys. At least 50 percent of all lots within the subdivision shall have alley loaded garages or parking areas (four points).</p>

            <p class="P3">c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;One hundred percent of residential units are all-electric (appliances are all-electric and a cold climate heat pump is provided) and no natural gas plumbing is constructed to serve the subdivision (three points).</p>

            <p class="P3">d.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Average dwelling units no larger than 1,800 square feet not including garage (three points).</p>

            <p class="P3">e.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A street network that connects at right angles to the greatest extent feasible with no cul-de-sacs or similar turnarounds. Blocks may not exceed 600 feet in length between intersections (two points).</p>

            <p class="P3">f.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Significant traffic calming design features selected from the <span class="italic">Engineering Design Standards</span> and Specifications for New Infrastructure (Table 13-10-002-02 &ndash; New Design and Retrofit of Existing Streets) as approved by the City Engineer (two points).</p>

            <p class="P3">g.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Detached garages located behind the primary structure on at least 50 percent of the lots within the subdivision (two points).</p>

            <p class="P3">h.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;All residential units within the subdivision include a minimum 80-square-foot front entry feature associated with the front entry door having a direct pedestrian connection from the front door to the sidewalk (one point).</p>

            <p class="P3">i.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Subdivision incorporates a combination of single-family, duplex, and/or multifamily units (two points).</p>

            <p class="P3">j.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The provision of recreational amenities within a park or Common Space area, including but not limited to dog parks, picnic areas, and sports courts (two points).</p>

            <p class="P3">k.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;At least 50 percent of the required resources per Division <a href="../Flagstaff10/Flagstaff1050090.html#10.50.90">10-50.90</a> are maintained within Common Space areas outside of individual lots (two points).</p>

            <p class="P3">l.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Front setbacks less than 15 feet for livable portions of the dwelling including the front entry feature (one point).</p>

            <p class="P3">m.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Attached street facing garages less than 50 percent of the width of the primary structure (one point).</p>

            <p class="P3">n.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Subdivision CC&amp;Rs and setback standards do not prohibit the development of accessory dwelling units (one point).</p>

            <p class="P3">o.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A minimum of 15 percent of all single-family dwelling lots include requirements for an accessory dwelling unit (one point for 15 percent, two points for 30 percent, three points for 50 percent).</p>

            <p class="P3">p.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Subdivision exceeds the minimum density of the applicable zoning district by at least one whole unit per acre (no fractions). For example, if the minimum density is two units per acre, the subdivision provides a minimum of at least three units per acre (one point for each whole unit over the minimum up to three points)</p>

            <p class="P3">q.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Subdivision includes enhanced pedestrian environments including outdoor seating areas or larger landscaping areas (one point for each).</p>

            <p class="HistoryNote">(Ord. 2023-28, Amended, 12/5/2023 (Res. 2023-57); Ord. 2019-32, Amended, 11/5/2019 (Res. 2019-49); Ord. 2019-22, Amended, 7/2/2019 (Res. 2019-31); Ord. 2016-07, Amended, 2/16/2016 (Res. 2016-02))</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="10.40.60.290"><a name="10.40.60.290">10-40.60.290</a> Quarrying Operations</h3>
            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="bold">Plans Required.</span></p>

            <p class="P2">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A plan of the area within a one-mile radius of site shall be prepared at a scale of 1,000 feet to the inch or less, with a 10-foot contour interval or less. There shall also be a plan of the proposed site at a scale of 100 feet to the inch or less, with a two-foot contour interval or less, showing all that is listed in Table 10-40.60.290.A., Plan of Area Requirements.</p>

